WIRE-SHAPE NOTE (honesty): the web `AuditLogEntry` interface names its columns
createdAt / action / resource / details, but the real backend
(internal/api/audit/log_handler.go -> internal/models/system.AuditLog) serializes
snake_case ts / actor / action / entity_type / entity_id / detail. The KMP shared
client returns the raw server JSON (no camelCase transform), so AuditLogPageModel.kt
reads the real wire keys and maps them onto the web's intended display semantics
(ts -> Time, entity_type[+entity_id] -> Resource, detail -> Details), with the web
aliases accepted as fallbacks. The page therefore renders real data rather than the
undefined fields the literal web property names would yield — no stubbing, ADR-011.

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps
':android' -> app/); the prompt snippet's ':app:' is the same module (the README gate
contract addresses ':android:'). Android SDK present (local.properties sdk.dir +
ANDROID_HOME), JDK 21, so the gate runs — not BLOCKED.

STRINGS NOTE (honesty): every visible literal resolves from res/values*/strings.xml via
stringResource (zero hardcoded text). The web string DEFAULTS are ported verbatim; the
Android resource keys live under the cohesive translation_auditLog_* namespace (the
established translation_<page>_* convention, mirroring translation_apiLogs_*). The
value <-> web-key mapping is enumerated in the PARITY section below. New keys were added
to values/, values-ar/ and values-he/ (ar/he ship the English fallback, exactly as the
i18n generator emits untranslated keys). MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are disabled
in the app lint config; lintDebug is green with these additions.

